# --- Terraform ---
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
# A `.tfvars` normally holds credentials, hence the blanket rule. `backend/infra/envs/`
# deliberately holds none: every secret in that configuration lives in Secrets Manager and
# Terraform never learns its value (ANV-40, `backend/infra/modules/secrets/main.tf`). The
# `local` / `dev` variable sets are the layout the ticket asked for and are worthless
# uncommitted, so they are excepted here — and `backend/tests/unit/test_infra_terraform.py`
# asserts both that this exception is still in place and that nothing secret-shaped has
# appeared in the files it uncovers.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
!backend/infra/envs/*.tfvars
# Backend configuration for the partial `backend "s3" {}` block. It names a real state
# bucket, so it is supplied at init time and never committed.
*.tfbackend

